WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.200
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:06.404
With Internet Access, Conditional Access
decides which security profile a user gets,

3
00:00:06.404 --> 00:00:09.262
and the profile decides
what the user can reach.

4
00:00:09.262 --> 00:00:13.036
It comes late in the run order
because it's separately licensed,

5
00:00:13.036 --> 00:00:17.899
and because an agency may keep its current
gateway; that's a decision from Module 1.

6
00:00:17.899 --> 00:00:20.438
T L S inspection comes last of all.

7
00:00:20.438 --> 00:00:23.199
It's the step most likely
to break applications,

8
00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:26.739
and the step most likely to read
content the agency shouldn't,

9
00:00:26.739 --> 00:00:30.350
so it starts only after filtering
works on server names alone.

10
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:34.569
In this module you build a pilot
security profile, govern every bypass,

11
00:00:34.569 --> 00:00:38.497
and then add inspection from a
dedicated certificate authority,

12
00:00:38.497 --> 00:00:41.260
within a scope the
privacy officer approved.
